    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0417" n="393" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg393"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fogg to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation.</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 29, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>One word additional to what I wrote you in my last despatch, relative to the
                    proposition for a treaty stipulation engaging United States consuls to afford
                    protection to Swiss citizens in those American States where the Swiss
                    Confederation may have no official representative.</p>
                <p>I learn that, by treaty engagements made long since, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >French</hi> consuls have been accustomed to afford the same kind of
                    protection, on application, to Swiss citizens in the east which they ask of the
                    United States consuls in the west. The <hi rendition="#italic">custom</hi> still
                    prevails. But how far it is now recognized as an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >obligation</hi> I am not at present enabled to say.</p>
                <p>With sincere regard, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE G. FOGG.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State of the U. S. of America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
